WEBVTT

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.630
The emergency assembly isn't just for us...

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.470
The Office of Space Development called...

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.130
They asked for you to go back to the Stellvia right away.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.440
It's been on the news, too...

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.730
It looks like fighting has broken out around the Ultima.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:05.180
Episode Fourteen: 
Dream and Reality

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.850
I wonder what's going to happen.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.180
It'll be all right.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.550
No reason to worry.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:23.310
Right.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.440
Welcome back!

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:49.450
Welcome back, welcome back! Welcome back!

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.600
I-I'm back.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.290
Without you here, Shipon, things were really boring.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.850
I'm so happy you came back early!

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.720
Arisa, somehow you seem normal.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:58.320
What?

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.810
Arisa, somehow you seem normal.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:01.820
What do you mean by that?

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:05.000
Well, there's a disturbance at the Ultima, right?

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.230
Oh, yeah, that does seem to be the case.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.360
I wonder if Rinna is all right.

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:13.590
See? It's not as serious as you thought, Shima-chan.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.360
What in the world are you talking about?

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.800
Well... since we were called back all of a sudden...

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.370
...I was wondering if something really horrible had happened.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:24.120
The people from the Big Four were with us, too.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.850
Oh, I see...

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.700
Hmm... I wonder what it is...

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.740
Things certainly do seem kind of unpleasant around here...

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.420
...but it's not that bad.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:33.400
Oh...

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:35.480
What?

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.940
Thank goodness.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:43.720
Let's go!
Right!

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:49.590
So where's my souvenir?

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.540
Oh, I was in a hurry, so...

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.760
Why, you!

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:53.840
Just kidding!

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:55.840
So what did you buy?

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.300
Well, first I bought some rice crackers and...

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:00.580
Thank you for coming all this way.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.260
You seem well.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:06.160
Do you have any new information?

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.130
So little I could use some.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:09.560
That is a problem.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.410
When I go back, I have to explain this to the congress.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:14.980
So which Foundation is it?

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.150
You certainly speak your mind.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.890
It's not like you believe that it's aliens, right?

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:24.470
There is too little information.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:27.530
The Stellvia is the front line for the Earth.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.350
I don't think I need to tell you that as the person at the very top...

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.100
...you have a duty to make the Earth's interests your foremost priority.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.190
I understand...

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.360
Ah... Thank goodness!

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:50.670
When I was told it was an emergency assembly, my heart skipped a beat.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.260
You are a worrier.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:56.160
We're in outer space, and we're still just students.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.680
There's no way anything is happening.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:00.380
That's true.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:04.830
Hot springs Manjyuu.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:06.920
Is it possible that this will taste like sulfur?

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.480
Sulfur? What kind of flavor is that?

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.850
It does have "hot springs" written on it, after all.

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.480
Now, now, don't think about it too much.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:19.580
You say that, but you don't know why it says "hot springs" either, do you?

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:23.570
It's delicious!

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:28.550
But since you didn't really have time to talk to your family...

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.440
...there was no point in going home.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.250
Really.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:37.130
But you did have the time to meet with Kouta's older sister.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:38.700
W-What's that supposed to mean?

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.290
Nothing at all.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:42.770
Meanie.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.310
Thank you for the food.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:45.090
Now then!

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:48.850
Shall we go and make a one-sided, five-hour-wait phone call to Rinna?

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:52.000
I wonder if Rinna's all right.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:53.130
Oh.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.390
She's still on the space transport.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.880
It takes forty days to get to the Ultima, after all.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:01.010
Oh, that's right!

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.190
So she's not wrapped up in this.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:04.870
Thank goodness.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.470
What have we been guiding the students for up until now?

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:14.960
So they can kill other people?

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:16.870
I'm telling you, you're worrying too much.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.350
There's no way it's a war.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:22.390
Then why did they call the students back?

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.570
And why only the ones who took part in the Great Mission?

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.500
It's because they're all excellent pilots.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.990
Well, I understand your point of view.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:35.140
But the Office of Space Development works for the government, right?

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.860
I'm sure that they're just gathering the students now...

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:41.360
...so that they don't get blamed later themselves.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.080
A lot of unnecessary things are happening.

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:53.420
Just for a minute, let's say your worries are correct.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.280
If that happened, the headmaster would do something about it.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.520
That's right. Nothing to worry about.

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:05.500
The power of a single teacher is insignificant...

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:22.280
She said she wants to be alone.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:24.360
All she needs is time then.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.930
This is Ayaka. She's sure to get back on her feet.

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:31.010
Until then, as long as this school continues to be a school...

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:32.140
What do you think?

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:35.290
Do you think it's the work of some other Foundation?

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.610
Surprisingly, it might actually be a show the Ultima is putting on itself.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:39.770
For what reason?

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:40.870
Who knows?

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:45.730
In any case, the most important point for us...

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:48.360
...is why we were called back here like this.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:54.980
With the conclusion reached at tomorrow's emergency meeting...

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:56.830
...depending on what that is...

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:00.500
...all of the dreams of this school might end.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:03.740
It's strange.

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.650
We're discussing it like this...

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:08.420
...but it feels like someone else's problem.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.430
How futile.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:41.190
I can't...

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:43.360
...hear anything.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:52.240
These changes aren't any better!

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:54.510
You're being loud.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:58.050
But I'm tired of this. I'm tired of this, tired of this, tired of eating this!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:08:59.980
Hmm?
Hmm?

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:04.760
Thank you very much.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:09.470
Sorry about this. You can't relax with your teacher here, right?

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:10.770
Of course not.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:14.560
If we're being treated, then we welcome anyone!

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:15.600
Right?

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:16.410
"Right"?

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:20.430
Sorry, but I can't give you guys any special treatment.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.230
Whoa, a serious reaction.

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:27.110
Sorry about calling you back during your vacation.

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:27.830
Oh, no...

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:30.780
Ma'am...
Hmm?

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:33.730
Are we going to have to fight?

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:39.800
I'd like to believe that's not the case.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:50.720
A strategy?

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:52.960
That is what they decided.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:56.030
In the same way that we created the Infinity...

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:59.300
...it wouldn't be surprising if the other Foundations...

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:00.390
...possessed something of their own as well.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.110
But even after saying that...

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:05.280
No one knows what to do.

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:07.650
That's what's happening right now.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:10.370
Humanity experienced the explosion from the supernova...

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.950
...and for the first time since the dawn of time, became one.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:15.800
But in the end...

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:17.940
...the concept of nations may have just been replaced...

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:21.040
...by the Foundations.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:27.980
Oh, everyone's coming back tomorrow.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.520
Somehow, it doesn't feel like a vacation at all.

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:36.280
Hey now, you're thinking unhappy thoughts again, aren't you?

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:38.500
Everyone's coming back...

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:42.210
...even though they weren't called, right?

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:44.230
I'm telling you, you're worrying too much.

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:45.820
It's all right.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.980
Would you mind acting like such a baby with Kouta instead?

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:53.660
Hey!

00:10:58.470 --> 00:10:59.530
It'll be all right.

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:02.130
Yeah... you're right.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.810
They're hot springs manjyuu.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:17.830
If you'd like, please eat them.

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:22.340
Thank you.

00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:29.750
Um, well, that is...

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:31.710
I'm sorry...

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:39.030
I'm sorry...

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:53.140
Let's begin.

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:56.250
Welcome back!

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.000
We're back!

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.990
Huh? Yayoi isn't with you?

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:11.390
She didn't want to be on the same flight as Pierre.

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:12.720
You're already saying that?

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:14.680
I'm so delighted to see you again.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:20.520
It seems like something serious is happening again.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.040
I wonder if the meeting has started already.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:25.580
I wonder what the unidentified objects are.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:27.090
Maybe U.F.O.s?

00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:27.980
I'm telling you...

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:31.170
...they're the secret weapons from some other Foundation.

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:35.300
For now, the battle at the Ultima is just a combat test.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:38.830
Infi has that something that really grabs you...

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:41.400
But the unidentified objects have an air of a conspiracy...

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:42.930
...so they're good, too, you know?

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:44.610
So you like that kind of thing?

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:48.600
Right! Guys are moved by that kind of thing.

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:49.380
Right?

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:53.520
Let's go eat something.

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:55.950
Yeah, I'm hungry.

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:59.190
The Fujiyama doesn't have meal service since we're so close, right?

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:06.390
W-What? What's wrong with talking about a man's romanticism?

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:10.990
I'm coming, too!

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:12.280
Wait for me!

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:17.520
No matter what the reason was for someone to attack the Ultima...

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.800
...it's obvious that a dangerous ideology exists.

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.300
We should arrange to be in a surveillance position immediately.

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.080
The threat from Hydrus Beta has passed.

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:28.330
There would be no problem if we turned...

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:31.340
...half of our surveillance facilities towards the other Foundations.

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:34.870
That would certainly save us time and money.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.340
What do you think?

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:40.020
Although, if we try to seize evidence...

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:43.250
...they could bring possible charges to the negotiation table.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:46.180
In that case, they could make us undergo a compulsory inspection!

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:49.150
For that, we should consult with the other Foundations.

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:51.150
Are you saying we should consult with the culprit?

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:53.090
I wonder.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:56.640
Isn't it a bit unreasonable to think that all the Foundations...

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:58.700
...are involved in this crime?

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.010
Are you saying this is the work of reactionary elements?

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:03.940
It is realistic to think that way.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:07.880
I don't think reactionary elements would have that kind of power.

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:08.640
Hmm...

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:12.230
It certainly does seem that there isn't enough information.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:14.570
Even still, there is something we can do.

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:18.100
Strengthen the security force.

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:22.210
Or depending on circumstances, establish a military space force.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.180
Unidentified crafts moving in fast.

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.350
Identifying them by their gravity response...

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:30.530
Ghosts.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.770
They're ID's as ghosts.

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:34.610
Security force, emergency launch.

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:36.030
They'll make contact in five minutes!

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:41.980
Hmm, two coffees.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:44.240
Hey, there's an opening all the way in. Lucky us!

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.590
A military space force is a rather bold suggestion.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:54.220
It looks like your jump in logic went too far, Mr. Hutter.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:57.050
Then what would happen if we were attacked right now?

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:59.360
The security force would deal with it.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.140
That's fine, if it's an opponent the security force can deal with...

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.300
This is Foundation Ultima airspace.

00:16:06.450 --> 00:16:08.330
Stop your flight immediately.

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:11.360
If you do not follow our instructions, we will open fire.

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:12.840
Two minutes until contact. We repeat.

00:16:13.190 --> 00:16:14.980
Stop your flight immediately.

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:27.820
I agree with the suggestion to strengthen the security force.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:31.520
However, it would be unreasonable to establish a military space force.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:35.390
It might cause an emergency situation instead.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:39.410
I understand what you're saying.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:44.270
But it's wrong to answer force with force.

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:46.820
That's clear when you look at history, isn't it?

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:51.380
If everyone thought like you do, then...

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.300
The Katies have locked on to the ghosts.

00:16:58.440 --> 00:16:59.110
Repeat, locked on.

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:00.870
The ghosts are changing course!

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:03.360
They're increasing speed as they head for the control boundary!

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.030
Seven daily specials!

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.980
Seven daily specials, correct? Thank you very much...

00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:10.530
Rice!

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.570
One extra big one!

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:14.260
One!

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:17.810
Yes, sir, one large rice, correct? Thank you very much.

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:20.120
So only the big Dai is getting a big rice?

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:25.420
The ghosts are leaving our controlled airspace.

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:30.070
The security force is going to level three alert.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:31.520
Level three.

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:37.560
I wonder if it's true that the Fujiyama is going to suspend its service?

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:39.960
There is that rumor.

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:44.040
But you all came back early because you were worried about that, right?

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:45.290
Just to be sure.

00:17:46.070 --> 00:17:48.870
There probably won't be a complete suspension of service.

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:51.160
But until the case with the Ultima is solved...

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.980
...they might lower the number of flights.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:56.420
I'd hate it if that happened.

00:17:56.620 --> 00:17:58.560
Yeah. It's better when things are peaceful.

00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:00.230
That's not it.

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:00.640
What?

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:04.200
Vegetables can only be grown on the Earth, right?

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:08.070
So if the shuttles stop flying, then I won't be able to eat them anymore.

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:10.960
You're worried about that?

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.930
Oh, but meals are vital.

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:17.930
I hope things will calm down soon...

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.190
A spoon might work better.

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:26.380
Thank you.

00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:35.310
Yes, yes, thank you for the food!

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:43.350
But seriously, your proposal was surprising, Mr. Hutter.

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:46.070
It is only right they should feel at least a mild sense of crisis.

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:49.200
Even still, aren't military preparations going a bit far?

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:51.100
Self-defense is, in a way, an instinct.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:55.580
It can be said that humanity has lost its survival instinct at the very least.

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:56.560
That is true...

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:01.570
It's true that it's natural for a living being to try to protect itself.

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:06.160
We may have forgotten that natural thing...

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:08.330
Our peace has made us complacent.

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:11.230
Mr. Richard.

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:12.040
Yes?

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:13.740
About what we discussed earlier...

00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:16.160
...could you please try and feel him out?

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:35.340
Welcome back...

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:40.580
Um...

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:46.690
Are you a new student?

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:49.420
Um, my name is Fujisawa.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:51.590
Um, nice to meet you.

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:55.900
Ayaka Machida.

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:00.300
Fujisawa... I'm Yayoi Fujisawa.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:02.780
I'm back.

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:16.900
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:16.900
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:16.900
Welcome back.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:26.060
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:26.060
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:17.900
Embrace the heart of blue in my arms. Welcome back.

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:18.570
I'm back.

00:20:26.060 --> 00:20:27.540
How did the meeting go?

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:30.510
It ended with the decision to have a joint session...

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:31.960
...with the other Foundations.

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.710
In the end, we just do as we're told.

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:37.250
I see...

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:39.110
Do you feel uneasy?

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:39.910
That is...

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:41.820
Hmm... Yeah, you would.

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:44.250
So you wanted to talk to me?

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:47.430
There's a new operating system that has been developed...

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:48.930
...exclusively for Infi.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:53.040
I was wondering if we could ask you to do the monitoring on it.

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:54.460
What do you think?

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:03.540
No way!

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:08.050
A development model of the D.L.S.? Is that being developed right now?

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:08.660
Yeah.

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:11.810
They said it's a system that directly processes...

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:12.680
...the information and your thoughts, or something.

00:21:14.010 --> 00:21:15.710
It sounds kind of fun!

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:19.120
What, is something funny?

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.190
Oh, nothing.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:22.680
I just thought that it's very much like you, Shima-chan.

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:25.920
It's incredible.

00:21:26.230 --> 00:21:27.970
Yeah, it really is incredible.

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:33.870
I might be able to feel the universe more directly.

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:36.800
Not that, you're the one that's incredible...

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:38.240
...for being chosen to do the monitoring.

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:39.910
Thanks.

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:54.080
I might be able to hear the glimmering.

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
Tabitatsu tsubasa te ni ire Kono sora mioroshite mitai no

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
I'll obtain wings to take off because I want to look down at this sky

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
飛び立つ翼手に入れ この空見下ろしてみたいの

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
Mirai wa dou agaitete mo Kanarazu otozureru kara

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
Even with how I'm struggling, I'll certainly visit the future

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
未来はどうあがいてても 必ず訪れるから

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
Dare mo mita koto no nai keshiki wo Nozonde shimau

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
I'm wishing for scenery that no one has seen

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
誰も見たことのない景色を 望んでしまう

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
Todomaru koto wo shiranai Fuan wo kakaeta yume wo

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
I don't know about things that stay put, or dreams that hold onto anxiety

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
とどまる事を知らない 不安を抱えた夢を

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
Ima wa kokoro omomuku mama ni dakou

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
Now let's embrace the proceeding spirit

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
今は心赴くままに抱こう

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
Naite warau tabi ni omou Atashi ga ikiteru imi wo

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
I cry every time I think you smile, I'll live for the meaning of it

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
泣いて笑う度に思う あたしが生きてる意味を

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
Hito wa maru de Irotoridori no hoshi no you da ne

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
People are completely multicolored like the stars, you know?

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
人はまるで 色とりどりの星のようだね

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
Kazaritateta you na kirei na yozora

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
The beautifully decked out night sky

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
飾り立てたような綺麗な夜空

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
Soshite mata Atashi wa miageta

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
And still I looked up

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
そしてまた あたしは見上げた・・・

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next episode

00:23:05.930 --> 00:23:07.120
This is Shima!
This is Arisa!

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:08.790
The opening ceremony started without any problems...

00:23:08.870 --> 00:23:09.860
...so now it's classes, classes!

00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:12.840
Oh-ho, so Miss Shima, you've become passionate about studying, have you?

00:23:12.900 --> 00:23:14.500
Or could it be that you're passionate about your love?

00:23:14.470 --> 00:23:16.200
Oh, no, what are you saying?

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:18.240
Look, he seems kind of slow on the draw, right?

00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:20.570
So for once, you should invite him to a movie or something, Shipon!

00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:22.240
What? R-Really?

00:23:22.310 --> 00:23:24.370
And then, all of a sudden, a crisis occurs!

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:24.820
What?!

00:23:25.140 --> 00:23:27.370
On the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe, "I Don't Understand".

00:23:27.620 --> 00:23:28.680
Please look forward to it!

00:23:28.750 --> 00:23:30.690
Hey, hey, what's the crisis?

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:31.870
I don't understand, I don't understand!

00:23:32.070 --> 00:23:34.910
I'm scared!

00:23:32.070 --> 00:23:35.050
Episode Fifteen: 
I Don't Understand I'm scared!
